// MISSION TEXT
Mission01=Vai all'aeroporto di Ridgeway
Mission01Desc=Ricordo quando queste montagne erano piene di villeggianti venuti dalla città. L'aeroporto di Ridgeway brulicava di gente. Guardalo ora! Un campo da gioco per gli zombie. Se hai bisogno di provviste, dovresti dargli un'occhiata.\n\nOrmai non parte più nessun volo ma ci sono buone opportunità di approvvigionamento ovunque.
Mission02=Vai a Badgers Hut
Mission02Desc=So many great memories were had here. A quaint little structure used by vacationers, Badger's Hut is now a zombie hangout. Blood covers the merry-go-round where children once played and the dead meander about waiting for their next travelling meal to stop and rest. \n\nFew scattered supplies can still be found here from the Hut's last visitors but no one has dared to venture there for quite some time. Most wouldn't, but in a pinch, those resources just may save your life.
Mission03=Vai alla Fattoria Barth
Mission03Desc=Il vecchio Willie Barth era l'esperto di cavalli del posto. Possedeva uno splendido cavallo che aveva chiamato Velluto per la sua criniera morbida e fluente. Il vecchio Willie uscì a vedere come stava Velluto dopo aver sentito dei rumori nel fienile. I dannati zombie la divorarono prima che Willie riuscisse ad arrivare alla porta.\n\nSfortunatamente anche lui subì la stessa sorte. È abbastanza poetico, se ci pensi. Un uomo e il suo cavallo, fianco a fianco, anche nella morte. Dovresti visitare la fattoria per porgere i tuoi ossequi, ma fai attenzione a non finire come il vecchio Willie e Velluto.
Mission04=Vai all'Accampamento Blue Ridge
Mission04Desc=Se ti dirigi a nord puoi trovare un rifugio sicuro tra le mura dell'accampamento Blue Ridge. Al suo interno puoi rifornirti di provviste all'emporio e lasciare gli oggetti del tuo Inventario globale. Puoi anche interagire con altri sopravvissuti sempre alla ricerca di scambi e baratti. Devi però stare attento ai dintorni dell'accampamento: i banditi si appostano vicino alle zone sicure. Questi maledetti opportunisti non hanno rispetto per nulla!\n\nSpero che non decida di seguire le loro orme, amico. Se lo fai, stai attento allo Sceriffo.
Mission05=Vai a Boulder City
Mission05Desc=Man, you must have either a death wish, or something seriously wrong with your head if you plan on heading to Boulder City. That place is infested to the max. Rescue chopper went in and never came out. Pilot and co-pilot were both eaten alive while the chopper went down. By the time the craft hit the ground they had already been disembowelled.\n\nGood luck making it back. 
Mission06=Vai a Campos City
Mission06Desc=Se prendi la sopraelevata e percorri ciò che rimane della tangenziale, potrai osservare le rovine della città ai tuoi piedi. Campos City sicuramente non è più attiva come un tempo ma ci sono sempre gruppi di sopravvissuti alla ricerca di provviste in giro. \n\nPresta molta attenzione quando entri in città, potrebbero esserci persone appostate su tetti che vigilano chi entra e chi esce dalla città. Se ti fai scoprire, il tuo viaggio potrebbe diventare molto breve.
Mission07=Vai a Camp Splinter
Mission07Desc=Una cosa è certa: non devi mai sottovalutare la possibilità di eventuali attacchi. Camp Splinter era un avamposto sicuro per i sopravvissuti, ma ben presto è stato conquistato dagli zombie. Chi ha potuto è fuggito, lasciandosi tutto alle spalle. Molti stavano dormendo al momento dell'attacco e sono stati divorati vivi nelle loro tende. Bel modo di svegliarsi, vero? Beh, se hai abbastanza palle come pensi puoi fargli una visita e recuperare un po' di provviste.\n\nStai attento, però: nemmeno i militari sono riusciti a proteggere Camp Splinter. Ed erano professionisti addestrati.
Mission08=Vai a Candlers Cabin
Mission08Desc=North of Crystal Lake lies Candlers Cabin. Abandoned many years ago, the cabin sits at the top of the map and sees very few visitors aside from the scattered zombies that have staked their claim on the land. \n\nAlbeit semi-dangerous, the trek up to Candlers Cabin could prove to be worth the risk.
Mission09=Vai all'Accampamento di Castle Pine
Mission09Desc=If you head South you can take safe refuge within the walls of Castle Pine Settlement. While you are there you can stock up on supplies from the General Store and pull items from your Global Inventory. You can also interact with other survivors should you be looking to barter and trade. Always be aware of your surroundings though, Bandits lurk near safe zones. Damn opportunists have no respect! \n\nHope you don't lead that life my friend. If you do, watch out for the Lawman.
Mission10=Travel to Hidden Forest Ranch
Mission10Desc=Before the infestation, the residence of Hidden Forest Ranch would complain about the noise from the airport on a regular basis. Now with the airport no longer operational I am sure they would be pleased by the silence, but instead the residents now spend their time wandering aimlessly looking for someone to eat.\n\nMosey on over to Hidden Forest Ranch and greet the locals.
Mission11=Vai a Clearview
Mission11Desc=Many a battles have been fought in Clearview since the outbreak. Some say rabies, others have a more biblical and supernatural reasoning for the infection. One thing is certain, no one is safe from its effect. Clearview is one of the most looted places in Colorado. There are zombies throughout the city but the more prevalent threat is that of the human kind. \n\nGive Clearview a go and see what you can come up with from looting. 
Mission12=Vai a Cottonwood Bend
Mission12Desc=Non c'è molto da vedere a Cottonwood Bend. Gli sciacalli hanno ripulito questo posto ma molti sono stati uccisi durante i loro tentativi, quindi potrebbero esserci oggetti sparsi intorno alle balle di fieno dei campi.\n\nPrendi la Statale 70 verso Cottonwood Bend ed esplora i dintorni alla ricerca di bottino.
Mission13=Vai a Crystal Lake Resort
Mission13Desc=Ahhh... il panorama pittoresco di Crystal Lake Resort. Acque limpide, accoglienti baite e... zombie? Generazioni di famiglie provenienti da ogni dove venivano in questa località  per rilassarsi. Ora c'è un inquietante silenzio nell'aria e il sangue ricopre i pavimenti delle baite che un tempo ospitavano i turisti in vacanza. Puoi prenderti tutto quello che riesci a trovare. Se hai problemi, corri verso il lago. Fortunatamente, gli zombie non sanno nuotare.\n\nVisita Crystal Lake Resort ed esplora le strutture dei dintorni alla ricerca di bottino.
Mission14=Vai alla Stazione dei ranger di Delta Peak
Mission14Desc=La torre delle comunicazioni è fuori uso, la stazione di polizia è deserta e nessuno si occupa più di spegnere gli incendi qui. L'espressione città fantasma non è sufficiente per descrivere la desolazione di questa zona. Voglio dire: almeno in una città fantasma nessuno cerca di mangiarti. Anche solo arrivare fino a qui è una missione suicida. Devi passare per alcune delle zone più pericolose del Colorado per raggiungere la stazione dei ranger di Delta Peak.\n\nPercorri la strada verso la stazione dei ranger di Delta Peak e fai del tuo meglio per rimanere vivo. 
Mission15=Travel to Milligan's Island
Mission15Desc=Sit right back, and you'll hear a tale, a tale of a fateful dip. A survivor went out one day, on a flimsy tip.  He was told there was a place to hide, he thought he'd get ahead.  What he found was a small island, and now he's very dead.\n\nFind Milligan's Island and poor Milligan's final resting place. 
Mission16=Vai al Complesso di Echo
Mission16Desc=Quando Smallville è stata invasa, i sopravvissuti si sono spostati a sud-ovest della città verso il complesso di Echo. Andava tutto per il meglio fino a quando qualcuno si è dimenticato di chiudere i cancelli del complesso. Non c'è bisogno di dire che il ragazzo non ha perso solo il lavoro a causa del suo errore. Il peggior portiere di sempre!\n\nIl suo disastro rappresenta un'opportunità per te. Dirigiti al complesso di Echo e raccogli tutto quello che trovi. Non ti preoccupare di chiudere la porta!
Mission17=Vai al rifugio di Emerald Peak
Mission17Desc=A two house lot overlooking zombie infested Smallville, Emerald Peak Retreat was the premier location for honeymooners looking to separate themselves from the hustle and bustle of the city and enjoy the scenic mountain views. Guess the honeymoon is over now that the zeds have made this their own. \n\nGet to Emerald Peak and snatch up what you can before the new tenants show up!
Mission18=Vai a Fallsdale
Mission18Desc=Il negozio di auto di Mel aveva i prezzi migliori sui ricambi per auto. Peccato che il povero Mel sia stato divorato mentre tentava di difendere il negozio. La gente dice che il suo corpo è ancora da qualche parte lì fuori. Il negozio è sempre lo stesso, ma adesso può costarti un'occhio della testa (letteralmente)!\n\nDirigiti a Fallsdale e recupera quello che ti serve per sopravvivere.
Mission19=Vai a Frosty Pines
Mission19Desc=Gli eventi di Frosty Pines rimarranno per sempre impressi nella memoria delle persone che sono sopravvissute all'attacco. I poveri sciatori che hanno perso la vita con il crollo della seggiovia si sono trasformati rapidamente in cibo per l'esercito dei morti viventi e senza anima che li aspettavano sotto. Tutti hanno abbandonato la stazione dirigendosi verso nord e lasciando via libera agli zombie.\n\nSe trovi il coraggio per visitare Frosty Pines, ti auguro un viaggio sicuro... pregherò per te.
Mission20=Vai a Glenwood Springs
Mission20Desc=Dicono che Glenwood Springs sia stata distrutta perché forse è stata l'origine dell'epidemia. Forse? Cioè... la città è stata rasa al suolo distruggendo le possibili informazioni sulle cause dell'epidemia. Per di più l'infezione si era già diffusa, quindi in realtà sono state distrutte solo le provviste per i sopravvissuti affamati. Nelle rovine fumanti della città si possono ancora trovare armi, cibo e altre suppellettili sparsi qua e là.\n\nVai a Glenwood Springs e cerca provviste tra le macerie.
Mission21=Vai all'accampamento di Goblin Peak
Mission21Desc=Se ti dirigi a est puoi trovare un rifugio sicuro tra le mura dell'accampamento di Goblin Peak. Al suo interno puoi rifornirti di provviste all'emporio e lasciare gli oggetti del tuo Inventario globale. Puoi anche interagire con altri sopravvissuti sempre alla ricerca di scambi e baratti. Devi però stare attento ai dintorni dell'accampamento: i banditi si appostano vicino alle zone sicure. Questi maledetti opportunisti non hanno rispetto per nulla!\n\nSpero che non decida di seguire le loro orme, amico. Se lo fai, stai attento allo Sceriffo.
Mission22=Vai a Hill Ranch
Mission22Desc=You used to hear the rooster's crow in the morning letting you know the morning had come again. The only thing that is heard now, are the low moans and groans from the undead that meander around the ranch.\n\nIf you need hand tools or a place to repair some of your gear you can find what you need at Hill Ranch. 
Mission23=Vai al Campeggio di Loco Mountain
Mission23Desc=Seems like forever ago that the cabins of Loco Mountain Campsite were filled with vacationing families. It was a beautiful site to see kids playing and everyone having a good time. You never would have been afraid the neighbour from the next cabin would be gnawing at your face while the rest of the pack dined on your family. \n\nIf you are feeling especially crazy, head over to Loco Mountain Campsite 
Mission24=Vai alla Fattoria Lonetree
Mission24Desc=Lonetree Farm's location left it semi-isolated from the rest of the towns so zombies waves were kept at a minimum. However, that also meant major troubles for the residents once those bastards actually made their way to the farm. \n\nMaybe you can go check out Lonetree Farm for clues to what happened and pick up supplies that may be lying around. 
Mission25=Vai a Mountain Crest
Mission25Desc=Mountain Crest is a good place to start looking for supplies. There is a market and pharmacy in town and plenty of houses and buildings to explore for weapons and defensive aid. There is also a shop in town where you can repair equipment that has degraded over time.\n\nSee what useful items you can find in Mountain Crest but just be warned that the zombie population is growing in numbers. 
Mission26=Vai alla Stazione metereologica di MT Massive
Mission26Desc=They may have been able to track the weather conditions over at Mt. Massive but there is no way they could have predicted the storm of death and destruction the infestation would bring. \n\nSee what you can find to help you survive at Mt. Massive Weather Station.
Mission27=Vai alla Base militare Norad
Mission27Desc=Drones are grounded and the entire base has be overrun by the living dead. Sure the looting is great here but you are risking it all by venturing out there alone. Countless lives have been lost but if you need weapons and supplies what other choice do you have?\n\nRaid Norad Military Base for supplies...if you dare. 
Mission28=Travel to Oak Mountain Rest Stop
Mission28Desc=Not likely that you will find a treasure chest of weapons here but there is a market and gas station you can check out for food and water. You might get lucky and find a few random weapons around the area but I wouldn't get to comfortable around there with them zeds roaming.\n\nScavenge for supplies at Oak Mountain Rest Stop.
Mission29=Vai a Parkerville
Mission29Desc=Zeds rolled through Parkerville like bats outta hell. Shut down that tiny town within minutes of their arrival. Few survivors made it out alive. The ones that escaped swam across the lake to get away.\n\nGo to Parkerville and investigate the town. 
Mission30=Vai alla Fattoria Patch
Mission30Desc=Patch farm has an eerie calm to it from a distance. Once those zeds get a whiff of live meat though, things get hairy real fast and that calm turns to panic instantly. \n\nTake what you can get from Patch Farm and get the hell out of there!
Mission31=Vai al Sito in cui si è schiantato un aereo cargo
Mission31Desc=A cargo plane went down delivering supplies to the airport. The crew was overtaken by a pack of zombies that got in through the cargo hold. Pilot was unaware of the impending doom until it was too late.\n\nInvestigate the Plane Crash near Ridgeway Airport 
Mission32=Vai a Pleasant Valley
Mission32Desc=It was a no brainer for the people of Pleasant Valley to evacuate the tiny town at first sight of the invasion. Luckily everyone made it out of the city safe. Unfortunately, they didn't make it far before being torn apart in the woods.\n\nSad, but at least Pleasant Valley is yours for the pillaging. 
Mission33=Vai a Rifle Ridge
Mission33Desc=Rifle Ridge is a particularly unkempt part of the Colorado landscape. Broken down cars, dirty bungalows and an abandoned RV complete with blood stained interior help give the area its character.\n\nMake your way to Rifle Ridge and search the area for supplies. 
Mission34=Vai a Rocky Ford
Mission34Desc=Rocky Ford is a decent area to go around looking for supplies. There are a couple of key places to loot and plenty of houses and buildings to explore for weapons and defensive aid. There is also a shop in town where you can repair equipment that has degraded over time. \n\nSee what useful items you can find in Rocky Ford but just be warned that the zombie population is growing in numbers. 
Mission35=Vai all'Avamposto dei sopravvissuti
Mission35Desc=Se ti dirigi a ovest puoi trovare un rifugio sicuro tra le mura dell'avamposto dei sopravvissuti. Al suo interno puoi rifornirti di provviste all'emporio e lasciare gli oggetti del tuo Inventario globale. Puoi anche interagire con altri sopravvissuti sempre alla ricerca di scambi e baratti.Devi però stare attento ai dintorni dell'accampamento: i banditi si appostano vicino alle zone sicure. Questi maledetti opportunisti non hanno rispetto per nulla!\n\n Spero che non decida di seguire le loro orme, amico. Se lo fai, stai attento allo Sceriffo. 
Mission36=Vai alla fattoria Shrute
Mission36Desc=Looking for places to loot huh? You could try Shrute Farm. Last I heard, various survival supplies could be found around the bales of hay that are in the fields and in surrounding buildings.\n\nHead North up Interstate 70 to Shrute Farm and scour the land for loot. 
Mission37=Vai a Sleepy Crest
Mission37Desc=Military personnel staked claim to Sleepy Crest after its residents were turned into the abominations you see walking the land. Now you can't step foot in there without that foot being ripped off and snacked on.\n\nCheck out the houses and military outpost in Sleepy Crest for survival gear.
Mission38=Vai a Smallville
Mission38Desc=Great opportunities for loot are all over this town. Police station has been abandoned but there are still weapons and ammo to be found. Not to mention all the other goodies left behind when the town went to hell.\n\nSee what Smallville has to offer and let's hope somebody doesn't have to save you! 
Mission39=Vai alla Proprietà di Smith
Mission39Desc=Hershel Smith lived alone and had a prime piece of real estate right on the lake. His kids were all grown and living their own lives in California. it was during his favourite home improvement show when he heard something at his front door. As he opened the door to see what was the matter, he was face to face with a creature unlike anything he had ever seen. Before he had a chance to react, Hershel was rushed by the flesh-eating creature at his door. The feeble old man was no match for the zombie...heartbreaking.\n\nGo to Smith's Estate and scavenge some supplies.
Mission40=Vai al Parco delle roulotte di Springer Ridge
Mission40Desc=For some reason, the dead are not attracted to Springer Ridge Trailer Park...yet. It's probably a good idea to make use of this before things change.  \n\nWait! Be careful up there. Man turns animalistic when desperate...awooooooo!
Mission41=Vai al Bivio superiore
Mission41Desc=Superior Junction is a sweet little area to go around looking for supplies. There are a couple of key places to loot and plenty of houses and buildings to explore for weapons and defensive aid. \n\nSee what useful items you can find in Superior Junction but just be warned that the zombie population is growing in numbers.
Mission42=Vai a Tyler Ranch
Mission42Desc=If you are looking for quick loot without having to go into big cities filled with zeds, take a look at Tyler Ranch. You can pick up some basic loot while there and maybe even a rifle the ranch hand left behind.\n\nGo to Tyler Ranch and search the area for supplies. 
Mission43=Travel to W. Boulder Meteorological Station
Mission43Desc=West Boulder Meteorological Station is a prime location to loot. You better hurry, once word spreads about this place, it will be a fight going and out of there. Just make sure to watch your back for zombies as well as humans.\n\nTravel to West Boulder Meteorological Station and stock up on supplies.
Mission44=Vai a Whitestone Mountain
Mission44Desc=Great opportunities for loot are all over this town. Place has been abandoned but there are still weapons and ammo to be found. Not to mention all the other goodies left behind when the town went to hell.\n\nSee what Whitestone Mountain has to offer and let's hope somebody doesn't have to save you! 
Mission45=Fabbrica il Cataplasma
Mission45Desc=Without any hospitals or medical centres around and the constant looting going on, bandages and other medical supplies are scarce. Good old American ingenuity is needed in these trying times. \n\nLocate blueprints to craft a Poultice and learn how to take matters into your own hands!
Mission46=Fabbrica l'Attutitore
Mission46Desc=Gli spari permettono sempre agli zombie e agli altri giocatori di individuare la tua presenza. Devi muoverti come un fantasma dentro e fuori le città per riuscire a sopravvivere. Passare inosservato ti sarà di grande utilità fino a quando avrai bisogno di usare la forza.\n\nTrova le istruzioni per fabbricare l'Attutitore e diventa un fantasma.
Mission47=Fabbrica la Fratellanza
Mission47Desc=It was a day unlike any other, El Guapo and his gang were outnumbered and out-gunned. Armed only with Canoe Paddles and Combat Knives, The Brotherhood manufactured the ultimate paddle by fusing the two weapons together and declaring war on any who challenged the band of survivors. \n\nLocate the blueprints to craft The Brotherhood and relive the glory of El Guapo!
Mission48=Fabbrica la Forza eccessiva
Mission48Desc=Poliziotti... pfui! Non avevano speranze contro l'orda degli zombie. Questi stupidi pulotti non erano preparati per un evento di questo tipo. Tutto quello che è rimasto di loro sono i Manganelli e qualche arma e fornitura qua e là. Fortunatamente qualcuno ha trovato un modo per trasformare i manganelli in un'arma mortale.\n\nCerca le istruzioni per fabbricare la Forza eccessiva e diventa il nuovo Giustiziere! 
Mission49=Fabbrica una Maschera antigas improvvisata
Mission49Desc=Senti un odore strano? Non sappiamo che effetto possano avere  i corpi bruciati degli zombie sugli esseri viventi. I sopravvissuti di un accampamento avevano redatto delle istruzioni per una Maschera antigas improvvisata, da fabbricare con oggetti comuni che si trovano nelle città abbandonate.\n\nCerca le istruzioni e proteggi i tuoi polmoni da Dio sa cosa!
Mission50=Fabbrica un Punteruolo
Mission50Desc=Probabilmente delle semplici forbici possono essere utilizzate come armi ma se la presa non è salda possono scivolarti dalle mani e persino romperti un dito se si aprono al momento dell'impatto. Come risolvere il problema? Con Stracci e Nastro isolante, naturalmente!\n\nCerca le istruzioni per fabbricare un Punteruolo e dai un nuovo significato all'espressione fai da te!
Mission51=Fabbrica il Bada Boom
Mission51Desc=Crazy folks messing with gun powder and whatnot making homemade explosives. it's reckless, dangerous and just might be crazy enough to save your life. \n\nLocate the blueprints to craft the Bada Boom! and try not to blow off your hands!
Mission52=Fabbrica il Piazza pulita
Mission52Desc="Quindi siamo arrivati a questo, eh? La vecchia scopa di mamma è diventata uno strumento mortale. Facciamo un po' di pulizia, mamma? Ci puoi scommettere!\n\nCerca le istruzioni per fabbricare il Piazza pulita e inizia a liberarti della spazzatura!
Mission53=Thinning the Threat
Mission53Desc=The zombie population has quickly grown out of control in key foraging areas around Colorado and we need survivors to help clear them out.  You look like a strong capable hunter, maybe you can help thin the threat.\n\nKill 5 zombies in Glenwood Springs, Frosty Pines, Fallsdale, Camp Splinter, Smallville, Clearview and Crystal Lake resort.
Mission54=Controllo della popolazione
Mission54Desc=It never ceases to amaze how many zombies still exist, and continue to appear every day.  If they had any sense of organization the living would have been wiped out years ago.  To ensure that we remain the dominant species we need to regularly thin their numbers.  \n\nHunt and kill 100 zombies.
Mission55=Uccidi gli zombie in formazione
Mission55Desc=Dalla prima apparizione di zombie in formazione, si è diffuso il timore che stessero diventando più intelligenti e apprendendo tecniche che nel tempo potessero portarli a collaborare per organizzare assalti alle loro prede o addirittura agli accampamenti sicuri. Gli studi hanno mostrato, però, che si tratta semplicemente del risultato del disorientamento provocato dalla pressione applicata sul timpano degli zombie dai tessuti circostanti. Ciò nonostante, sono fastidiosi e devono essere uccisi.\n\nCerca e uccidi 10 zombie in formazione per ricevere una ricompensa.
Mission56=Uccidi gli zombi velocisti
Mission56Desc=L'unica cosa peggiore degli zombie velocisti che ci si può immaginare sono i ragni volanti. I primi purtroppo però esistono e bisogna occuparsene. Anche con un'arma completamente carica possono rappresentare una sfida, il che li rende una minaccia pericolosissima per i sopravvissuti inesperti.\n\nCerca e uccidi 10 zombie velocisti per ricevere una ricompensa."
Mission57=Uccidi gli zombi urlatori
Mission57Desc=Se la tua prima reazione nell'ascoltare il raccapricciante urlo degli "urlatori" è quella di correre, potresti allontanarti dal pericolo, ma la fuga potrebbe non essere sufficiente. Il suono penetrante delle grida degli urlatori attirerà l'attenzione di tutti gli altri zombie della zona e presto potresti ritrovarteli addosso.\n\nCerca e uccidi 10 zombie urlatori per ricevere una ricompensa.
Mission58=Uccidi il super zombie
Mission58Desc=For as long as many of us can remember, there have been stories of a zombie so large so powerful that it could smash through barricades like they were made of paper, and devour a man whole.  No one has been able to prove the existence of this monstrosity, until recently when the blood-curdling sound of its call could be heard in the night, and the remains of hunting parties have been found as unrecognisable heaps of gore.  \n\nSeek out and kill the elusive, and devastatingly powerful Super Zombie.  We suggest you bring your friend... all of them.
Mission59=Forniture di Blue Ridge: acqua
Mission59Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Blue Ridge safe settlement is in need of clean drinking water.  \n\nDeliver 5 bottles of 375ml Water to the Blue Ridge safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission60=Forniture di Blue Ridge: cibo
Mission60Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Blue Ridge safe settlement is in need of more food.\n\nDeliver 5 bags of Chips to the Blue Ridge safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission61=Blue Ridge Supplies: Bandages
Mission61Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Blue Ridge safe settlement is in need of more bandages.\n\nDeliver 5 bandages to the Blue Ridge safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission62=BONUS: Blue Ridge Demilitarization
Mission62Desc=If the zombies weren't bad enough, we have seen a massive rise in person to person violence due to a rush for armaments.  The safe settlements are proposing a bit of a demilitarization, encouraging survivors to turn in their weapons for less violent goods.\n\nDeposit 1 VSS sniper rifle into the Garbage Bin in the Blue Ridge safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission63=Forniture di Goblin Peak: acqua
Mission63Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Goblin Peak safe settlement is in need of clean drinking water.\n\nDeliver 5 bottles of 375ml Water to the Goblin Peak safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission64=Forniture di Goblin Peak: cibo
Mission64Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Goblin Peak safe settlement is in need of more food.\n\nDeliver 5 bags of Chips to the Goblin Peak safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission65=Goblin Peak Supplies: Bandages
Mission65Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Goblin Peak safe settlement is in need of more bandages.\n\nDeliver 5 bandages to the Goblin Peak safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission66=BONUS: Goblin Peak Demilitarization
Mission66Desc=If the zombies weren't bad enough, we have seen a massive rise in person to person violence due to a rush for armaments.  The safe settlements are proposing a bit of a demilitarization, encouraging survivors to turn in their weapons for less violent goods.\n\nDeposit 1 Blaser sniper rifle into the Garbage Bin in the Goblin Peak safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission67=Forniture di Castle Pine: acqua
Mission67Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Castle Pine safe settlement is in need of clean drinking water.\n\nDeliver 5 bottles of 375ml Water to the Castle Pine safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission68=Forniture di Castle Pine: cibo
Mission68Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Castle Pine safe settlement is in need of more food.\n\nDeliver 5 bags of Chips to the Castle Pine safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission69=Castle Pine Supplies: Bandages
Mission69Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Castle Pine safe settlement is in need of more bandages.\n\nDeliver 5 bandages to the Castle Pine safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission70=BONUS: Castle Pine Demilitarization
Mission70Desc=If the zombies weren't bad enough, we have seen a massive rise in person to person violence due to a rush for armaments.  The safe settlements are proposing a bit of a demilitarization, encouraging survivors to turn in their weapons for less violent goods.\n\nDeposit 1 M107 sniper rifle into the Garbage Bin in the Castle Pine safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts."
Mission71=Forniture dell'Avamposto dei sopravvissuti: acqua
Mission71Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Survivalist Outpost safe settlement is in need of clean drinking water.\n\nDeliver 5 bottles of 375ml Water to the Survivalist Outpost safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission72=Forniture dell'Avamposto dei sopravvissuti: cibo
Mission72Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Survivalist Outpost safe settlement is in need of more food.\n\nDeliver 5 bags of Chips to the Survivalist Outpost safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission73=Survivalist Outpost Supplies: Bandages
Mission73Desc=There is a reason the safe settlement are able to remain safe, and that is constant upkeep by survivors like yourself.  The Survivalist Outpost safe settlement is in need of more bandages.\n\nDeliver 5 bandages to the Survivalist Outpost safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission74=BONUS: Survivalist Outpost Demilitarization
Mission74Desc=If the zombies weren't bad enough, we have seen a massive rise in person to person violence due to a rush for armaments.  The safe settlements are proposing a bit of a demilitarization, encouraging survivors to turn in their weapons for less violent goods.\n\nDeposit 1 SIG Sauer 556 assault rifles into the Garbage Bin in the Survivalist Outpost safe settlement, and receive a reward for your efforts.
Mission75=Maestria con le armi: mani nude
Mission75Desc=Do you think you have what it takes to be a master of the fist?  Bare knuckle box your way through the undead and perfect the art of fistery on those menacing brain-eaters! \n\nProve your skill by killing 20 zombies using nothing but your hands.
Mission76=Maestria con le armi: armi bianche
Mission76Desc=Qualsiasi zoticone è in grado di sparare con un'arma e uccidere uno zombie. Per uccidere uno zombie con un'arma bianca, invece, bisogna essere un uomo vero esperto in combattimenti, mi capisci? \n\nDimostra le tua abilità uccidendo 20 zombi solo con armi bianche.
Mission77=Maestria con le armi: pistole
Mission77Desc=Ehi amigo...? Sei bravo a utilizzare la pistola? \n\nDimostra le tue abilità uccidendo 20 zombie solo con pistole.
Mission78=Maestria con le armi: fucili
Mission78Desc=Ci salveranno le pallottole, non gli abbracci! È arrivato il momento di far saltare la testa a quei bastardi! \n\nDimostra le tue abilità uccidendo 20 zombie solo con fucili.
Mission79=Maestria con le armi: fucili mitragliatori
Mission79Desc=Put those close range pea shooters to work and eliminate some of the zombie threat by popping off sub machine gun rounds in their freaking heads!\n\nKill 20 zombies using only Sub Machine Guns
Mission80=Maestria con le armi: mitragliatrici
Mission80Desc=Ratta-tat-tat on a dead man's cap! Why fire a few shots when you can demolish an entire group of zeds with a barrage of firepower through machine gun bullets filling the air.\n\nKill 20 zombies with Machine Guns and light up the night!
Mission81=Maestria con le armi: fucili da assalto
Mission81Desc=Semi-automatico, completamente automatico o a colpo singolo? Scegli il tuo preferito e manda all'altro mondo questi scherzi della natura! \n\nDimostra le tue abilità uccidendo 20 zombie solo con fucili d'assalto.
Mission82=Maestria con le armi: fucili da cecchino
Mission82Desc=Perché rischiare avvicinandoti al nemico? È ora di fare pratica utilizzando degli obiettivi mobili semi-viventi. \n\nDimostra le tue abilità uccidendo 20 zombie solo con fucili da cecchino.
Mission83=Maestria con le armi: granate
Mission83Desc=Gli zombie sono attirati da qualsiasi rumore. Fagli sentire un bel botto, lanciandogli addosso una granata. \n\nDimostra le tue abilità uccidendo 20 zombie solo con le granate.
Mission84=Find Wooden Barricade
Mission84Desc=The tree's have more use then just being paper. Have to find a way to sturdy my defense using them.\n\nObtain 1 Wooden Barricade. 
Mission85=Find Antibiotics
Mission85Desc=Feeling really sick. A little woozy now.  If only there was something i could take. The infection is starting to get worse.\n\nObtain 1 Antibiotic.
Mission86=Find Bandages
Mission86Desc=Sliced my hand open and now I'm bleeding all over the place. If only i had something to wrap this.\n\nObtain 1 Bandage. 
Mission87=Find Bandages DX
Mission87Desc=It's a gusher. Didn't have a choice had to run through the barb wire. Going to need more then your standard Bandage.\n\nObtain 1 Bandages DX
Mission88=Find Pain Killers
Mission88Desc=It aches all over my body. That was a long fall. Feeling so numb and slowing down. Need something to hold me over and fight through the pain till I can reach safety.\n\nObtain 1 container of Pain Killers.
Mission89=Find Medkit
Mission89Desc=Going to need a lot for this trip. I can only imagine that there is a lot of pain in my future. Going to need something that can keep me extremely healthy. Must stay on my toe's.\n\nObtain 1 Medkit.
Mission90=Find Bag of Chips
Mission90Desc=Crunchy, salty, flavourful bags of baked potato goodness. It can only remind me of the good old days when running constantly wasn't necessary. So hungry.\n\nObtain 1 Bag of Chips
Mission91=Find Instant Oatmeal
Mission91Desc=Opening that box, pulling out the packet, and shaking it. Pouring the contents in the lilttle paper baggy into the bowl and adding hot water. Breakfast is served.\n\nObtain 1 Instant Oatmeal.
Mission92=Find Chocolate Bar
Mission92Desc=Nothing satisfies your hunger like an aged chocolate bar found on the ground near a pile of zombie carcasses. Don't be such a diva...you would be surprised at what man can eat when in desperate times. \n\nObtain 1 Chocolate Bar
Mission93=Find Granola Bar
Mission93Desc=It ain't a steak but at least it ain't grubworms! Besides, granola is supposed to be old and dry. Make sure you have some water to wash it down.\n\nObtain 1 Granola Bar
Mission94=Find Can of Tuna
Mission94Desc=It isn't a chicken or a fish...it's all you got left in the cupboard and by golly, you will eat every last bit of it to survive. \n\nObtain 1 Can of Tuna
Mission95=Find MiniSaints
Mission95Desc=Care for an expired pack of two-stick donutty goodness? Well what are you waiting for? Grab some MiniSaints and cross your fingers there aren't creepy crawlers inside.\n\nObtain 1 pack of MiniSaints 
Mission96=Find Coconut Water
Mission96Desc=Well, we won't be taking any tropical getaways anytime soon. Closest thing we have to a tropical island getaway is the delicious refreshing taste of Coconut Water. \n\nObtain 1 Coconut Water
Mission97=Find Energy Drink
Mission97Desc=Killing zombies and looting takes a lot out of you. \n\nObtain 1 Energy Drink
Mission98=Find Electro-AID
Mission98Desc=Running from zombies and other humans can take it's toll on your body. Make sure you maximize your potential with Electro-Aid and keep your engine firing on all cylinders! \n\nObtain 1 Electro-Aid
Mission99=Find Can of Soda
Mission99Desc=Makes perfect sense to drink a random can of cola found in an abandoned store or restaurant. I mean, it is only corrosive if you leave something in it. Drinking it is fine, right? \n\nFind a Can of Soda
Mission100=Find Juice
Mission100Desc=Drink it while you can. There are zero fruit trees around and no supply trucks coming into any of the safe zones. Who would have thought Juice would have hit the black market?\n\nFind a bottle of Juice
Mission101=Find Water 1L
Mission101Desc=Plan for a journey, pack for survival. Make sure that you have enough Water to hydrate yourself when your thirst and stamina get low. You will need to be combat ready at all times. \n\nFind Water 1L
Mission102=Find Water 375ml
Mission102Desc=Plan for a journey, pack for survival. Make sure that you have enough Water to hydrate yourself when your thirst and stamina get low. You will need to be combat ready at all times. \n\nFind Water 375ML
Mission103=Find Can of Pasta
Mission103Desc=My noodle has a first name, it's E X P I R E D! In these trying times, beggars cannot be choosey. Slurp that noodle like it was your last! \n\nFind a Can of Pasta
Mission104=Find Can of Soup
Mission104Desc=No bowls, spoons or even crackers. Just a straight up can of soup. Almost like mom used to prepare for you only slightly passed it's expiration date. Better than dying of starvation and turning into one of those...things. \n\nFind a Can of Soup 
Mission105=Find Can of Ham
Mission105Desc=Time to go Hard As a Mother, and find some real food.  None of that soupy stuff, or sugary snacks.  You need to find yourself some HAM.\n\nObtain 1 Can of Ham.
Mission106=Find Bag MRE
Mission106Desc=If it's good enough for a soldier it is good enough for me. Satisfying my every need and giving me the strength to go on. This is the meal of choice for a one man army.\n\nObtain 1 Bag MRE
Mission107=Find C01-Vaccine
Mission107Desc=With all these zombies around it is only a matter of time before you, or someone you care about, will get infected.  If you do not react quickly, the infection will spread and kill the host.  With a vaccine you can slow or even stop the process.\n\nObtain 1 C01-Vaccine.
Mission108=Find C04-Vaccine
Mission108Desc=With all these zombies around it is only a matter of time before you, or someone you care about, will get infected.  If you do not react quickly, the infection will spread and kill the host.  With a vaccine you can slow or even stop the process.\n\nObtain 1 C04-Vaccine.
Mission109=Find Barb Wire Barricade
Mission109Desc=You may not be able to stop them, but you can sure as hell slow them down with a barbed wire barricade, so stock up.\n\nObtain 1 Barb Ware Barricade.
Mission110=Find Riot Shield
Mission110Desc=When you are stuck inside a building and surrounded by zombies, a good riot shield can mean the difference between life an death.\n\nObtain 1 Riot Shield
Mission111=Find Sandbag Barricade
Mission111Desc=You may not be able to stop them, but you can sure as hell slow them down with a sandbag barricade, so stock up.\n\nObtain 1 Sandbag Barricade.
Mission112=Find Flare
Mission112Desc=Flares are spectacular for eliminating dark areas, and revealing enemies in the dark.  They are also great tools for luring zombies away from your desired path.\n\nFind 1 Flare.
Mission113=Find Chemlight White
Mission113Desc=It gets scary out here alone in the dark. I wish i could see even if it's just a few feet in front of me. So i can pierce a bit of this darkness. \n\nObtain 1 Chemlight White.
Mission114=Find Chemlight Green
